{
  "about": "Shared cases for the instructor teaching-time rule semantics. core/services/instructor_availability.py and static/js/instructor-time-rules.js must both pass every probe, open count and summary. 'open' counts default lecture/lab periods (7 lecture and 5 lab columns, Sun-Thu) not blocked by the rules. 'summary' is the API's 'open' object for the rule set on the default grid, derived BY HAND from the grid (lecture 09:00-10:15, 10:30-11:45, 10:50-12:05, 13:00-14:15, 14:30-15:45, 14:45-16:00, 16:00-17:15; lab 09:00-10:40, 10:45-12:25, 13:00-14:40, 14:45-16:25, 16:30-18:10): days.lecture/days.lab[d] = day d has an open period of that grid; a shape is feasible iff its meetings fit on distinct days each with an open period of its grid (75 min -> lecture, 100 min -> lab); no_teaching_days = no open lecture AND no open lab period; state any (every period open) / none (no period open) / narrow (some shape infeasible) / limited. Never record these from the code. Rules are in the editor's wire format.",
